---
// The mark as the panel's masthead — mark, name, facts, address, in reading order.
//
// It used to live in a centred `nav.topbar` in Layout.astro (chooser:
// andrewshiau-panel-shape, Q1/02, moved it here). The figure itself is now MarkFigure.astro,
// shared with the case-study marker so the two drawings can't drift.
//
// TWO call sites, not ten: the index and /gate/. The eight case-study panels dropped it
// (chooser: andrewshiau-panel-marks, Q5/06) — their side marker draws the same figure, so
// their panel head was the figure twice, stacked, and the marker became the link home
// instead. What's left here is the pages whose panel has no side marker to carry it.
//
// `home` is false on the index, because a link to the page you are already on is a link that
// does nothing — there the mark is the masthead, not navigation. /gate/ is a real elsewhere,
// so there it links, and the accessible name lives on the anchor: the figure is decorative
// once its wrapper is named, and a `role="img"` inside a labelled link announces twice.
import MarkFigure from './MarkFigure.astro';
interface Props { home?: boolean }
const { home = true } = Astro.props;
---
{home ? (
  <a class="pmark" href="/" aria-label="andrewshiau — home"><MarkFigure /></a>
) : (
  <div class="pmark" aria-hidden="true"><MarkFigure /></div>
)}
